    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# 8. Generating explanations for model predictions using LIME"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "N1S4_TeRn-oi"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 8.1. Generating explanations on 2015 Panel 20 deployment data\n",
        "This section shows how LIME can be integrated with AIF360 to get explanations for model predictions."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "KxwAhoa4oBEf"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "train_dataset = dataset_transf_panel19_train  # data the deployed model (lr from transformed data)\n",
        "test_dataset = dataset_orig_panel20_deploy  # the data model is being tested on\n",
        "model = lr_transf_panel19  # lr_transf_panel19 is LR model learned from Panel 19 with Reweighing\n",
        "thresh_arr = np.linspace(0.01, 0.5, 50)\n",
        "best_thresh = thresh_arr[lr_transf_best_ind]"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "qkqppBWYn6kc"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "First, we need to fit the encoder to the aif360 dataset"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7ZqRs1t0oI0O"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "lime_data = LimeEncoder().fit(train_dataset)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "8pwBgNJXoGnf"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The transform() method is then used to convert aif360 features to LIME-compatible features"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Mq7gYcbRoMR0"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "s_train = lime_data.transform(train_dataset.features)\n",
        "s_test = lime_data.transform(test_dataset.features)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "eX4S1_VFoKbX"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The LimeTabularExplainer takes as input the LIME-compatible data along with various other arguments to create a lime explainer"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ZAK4Tc90oQGt"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "explainer = LimeTabularExplainer(\n",
        "        s_train, class_names=lime_data.s_class_names,\n",
        "        feature_names=lime_data.s_feature_names,\n",
        "        categorical_features=lime_data.s_categorical_features,\n",
        "        categorical_names=lime_data.s_categorical_names,\n",
        "        kernel_width=3, verbose=False, discretize_continuous=True)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "HtTiK5s-oOJE"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The inverse_transform() function is used to transform LIME-compatible data back to aif360-compatible data since that is needed by the model to make predictions. The function below is used to produce the predictions for any perturbed data that is produce by LIME"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Dohv7vRXoThT"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "def s_predict_fn(x):\n",
        "    return model.predict_proba(lime_data.inverse_transform(x))"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "DG11kB3FoRt4"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The explain_instance() method can then be used to produce explanations for any instance in the test dataset\n",
        "\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "nuWWV8mGoW-W"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "def show_explanation(ind):\n",
        "    exp = explainer.explain_instance(s_test[ind], s_predict_fn, num_features=10)\n",
        "    print(\"Actual label: \" + str(test_dataset.labels[ind]))\n",
        "    exp.as_pyplot_figure()\n",
        "    plt.show()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "9SmbVca4oVQC"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "print(\"Threshold corresponding to Best balanced accuracy: {:6.4f}\".format(best_thresh))\n",
        "show_explanation(0)\n",
        "show_explanation(2)"
      ],
